# Storm Active Work + Global Todo (vault tracking)

Maintain live checklists in the **personal** vault using the Storm MCP:
`Storm/Active Work.md` is the short in-flight queue and `Storm/Global Todo.md`
is the one aggregate view (milestones, Agent Runtime phases, in-flight,
backlog, parking lot). `PLAN.md` remains the decision log and milestone record.

## When to touch them

- Starting a multi-step Storm task: read Active Work first (`list_vaults` →
  `search` query `Active Work` → `get_note`), and skim Global Todo
  (`Storm/Global Todo.md`).
- Finishing or blocking an item: `get_note` then `update_note` with the same
  `base_version` — check off done work, add new open items, note blockers.
  Update **both** Active Work (queue) and Global Todo (aggregate) when a
  milestone, phase, or queue item changes state.
- Do not leave the only status in a chat transcript.

## How

1. Vault id from `list_vaults` (name `personal`).
2. Find the note with `search` (`Active Work` / `Global Todo` or their paths).
3. Always `get_note` before `update_note`; send back full markdown + `base_version`.
4. Keep Active Work short: **Now** / **Done recently** / **Parking lot**. Link
   companion notes with wikilinks (`[[Storm Releases]]`, etc.). Global Todo
   mirrors state rather than replacing it.

## Do not

- Duplicate the whole of `PLAN.md` into the vault notes.
- Create a second competing todo note; update these.
- Skip the update because the repo `PLAN.md` already changed — update all when
  the active queue moved.
